 darren's ever since i  saw requiem for a dream when i was a  college freshman  writing my first plays and i'm so  grateful that he's bringing his singular  talent and his vision to this film  today we're celebrating the release of  the kid detective by talking to the film  star adam brody  adam thanks for coming on weekly ticket  man thanks for having me  now you've been attached to this film  for quite some time what drew you to the  role  the strength of the writing uh evan  morgan writer director he's just got a  very sharp  very funny very melancholic unique voice  and then  i love the premise it's a high concept  premise and a you know low budget movie  a heightened world and so it plays with  on one hand this very hollywood sort of  idea and on the other hand low budget  movie and a lot of hidden  depth and it's comedic it's dramatic  it's just so many things that that i  really respond to but mostly  above all he's just great writer is it  hard to balance that sort of  humor with the darker undertones like  murder and kidnapping  yeah very much and in fact we had a lot  of productive clashes throughout the  filming of it where  uh you know he'd always bring it down  and i would always kind of want to  play a little and he'd want it more  subdued and i think we ended up kind of  in the middle  so you know it was a successful  collaboration but it was a constant  negotiation  is there one scene that you're uh you're  glad that you got to kind of  bring to your level mostly he pulled it  to his level but  he he won on most of it and i just  thought well this movie's going to live  or die with his  the strength of his you know choices  either he's right or  if he's wrong and i'm right the movie's  still not going to be good because he's  either got to have it or he doesn't so  i'll  mostly acquiesce to him but um you know  there's a few  a bit of there's a couple yells that  were mine and  i told let's even in edits was like  let's try that or let's put that one  back in and so  the few times i raised my voice i'm  happy that's in there but mostly he won  well they can release like a yell  edition that's yeah yeah  yeah yeah yeah all right cool um so  there's so many detective films out  there what do you think makes a good  detective film  you know i don't watch them as puzzles  necessarily personally you know i i  some people do some people are all about  trying to solve and that you know i  i want to be surprised at the end i want  to not see it coming  but i don't even have to really follow  the how or why of it  you know some of my favorite ones i i  don't understand  but i just think colorful characters i  think you got to have  colorful characters and you got to have  danger and you got to have humor  mostly you don't always have to have  humor but i think most of my favorites  do  certainly some great ones don't have are  pretty dead serious so i guess it  depends if you're going if it's leaning  more comedy or more  you know the the less comedic you are  the more it's gonna have to be the  straight you know lean into the strength  of the  story if you thought i was gonna let you  get away without telling me what some of  your favorites  are you got another thing coming what  are your favorites well chinatown on one  hand  we talked a lot about the long goodbye  with this movie we like the longer bylaw  and that's you know  dark but has you know real comedic you  know a lot of comedy in there too  kiss kiss bang bang has been a favorite  for a long time  yeah you know i saw this one a couple  years ago gemini i saw it on a plane it  was so good  small one with lola kirk is her name and  zoe kravitz and i thought it was great  there's another small detective one that  i i really enjoyed well you know a lot  of us are spending a lot of time at home  is there any movie that you've streamed  at home that you've particularly enjoyed  earlier this year of new movies i like  the invisible man a lot i thought that  was good  it was just like good popcorn it's a  good hollywood horror movie it was  neat this year honestly i'd never seen  sound of music  and now i've seen it like 20 times  mostly because my daughter but also it's  like my favorite movie it's just the  best  which song from that movie gets stuck in  your head the most would you say  um that's a good question they rotate on  what my  what what the crew is singing around my  house like it sort of rotates they're  all  really but i mean that's the strength of  a good musical is that they all  you know they all have their moment and  so i can't say  one more than the other all right man  well uh thanks for talking to us  all right i appreciate it thanks a lot  available to watch at home today is the  kid detective  so what can i help you with somebody  murdered my boyfriend  seriously pretty seriously he was  stabbed 17 times  a once celebrated kid detective  continues to solve the same trivial  mysteries between hangovers and bouts of  self-pity  but a naive client brings him his first  adult case  to find out who brutally murdered her  boyfriend the film stars adam brody  sophie nelisse and sarah sutherland  and available to watch at home today is  the climb  mike's in the living room he got fat  right yeah  merry christmas rich scissors  oh my god is that mike you got fat  kyle and mike are best friends who share  a close bond until mike sleeps with  kyle's fiance  the film follows their tumultuous but  enduring relationship across many years  of laughter  heartbreak and rage it's also the story  of real-life best friends who turn their  profound connection into a rich film  about the boundaries or lack thereof  in all close friendships alright well  that's it for today but leave us a  comment and let us know what you'll be  watching this week  i'm kale and i'll see you next time  [Music]

